  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enguri HPP Phase V - Georgia: Enguri HPP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;Proposed Enguri HPP rehabilitation project is an essential part of the infrastructure improvement required to support the country&#xBF;s economic development and improved energy security. Moreover, the rehabilitation of Enguri dam and increase in the Plant&#xBF;s generation would assist Georgia&#xBF;s transformation into an electricity hub and potentially integrate it into the EU&#xBF;s internal electricity market, further diversifying EU&#xBF;s energy supplies. The Project delivers strong climate change mitigation benefits through increasing efficiency of a major hydro power plant. Rehabilitation will result in additional renewable energy generation, reduction in water leakages as well as GHG emission savings. EU grant contribution also concerns the biodiversity conservation related activities. The fish pass on the Enguri river would seek to achieve relevant biodiversity protection objectives and will concern the segment downstream of the Enguri Dam where other smaller-scale barriers exist. Thus, the rehabilitation efforts carry high significance in terms of biodiversity conservation. At regional level, the Project is in line with the Black Sea Submarine Cable Project.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
